cmp against vanilla vendor/pointers.js at sync-base 939a8f1: NOT
byte-equal. Vanilla's bin/build-pointers.sh, run on this worktree with
esbuild 0.17.19, 0.19.12, 0.21.5, 0.23.1, 0.24.2, 0.25.0, 0.25.12,
0.26.0, 0.27.7 and 0.28.2, gives 277337-277591 bytes; vanilla's bundle
is 278654 bytes. Both bundles embed commit
ec7a81386baaa372134bf90662890a114436afd4, and both have the same set
of string literals and identifiers from the library (isMemory, isCode,
isBase, isSlice, isTwoOperands, "Region not found", keccak256, ...).
The difference is in the bundled yaml code: vanilla's keeps 420
`const` declarations that every esbuild version above turns into `let`
when it minifies. So vanilla's bundle was built from another checkout's
node_modules or with another tool; the library code is the same commit.

Decision (gnidan, 2026-10-07): the pin need not be byte-equal to
vanilla's bundle; "parity is dependent on behavior, not bundle bytes".
The gate is src/engine/lib.parity.test.ts (in npm test): vanilla's
vendor/pointers.js at sync-base against lib.ts, for every state
variable and every players[key] of the four fixtures at both points
(48 dereferences): identical regions (name, location, slot, offset,
length) and identical bytes read; and some expressions evaluate the
same.
